# [CR#205.4d,704.5j] "If two or more legendary permanents with the same name are controlled by the
# same player, that player chooses one of them, and the rest are put into their owners' graveyards.
# This is called the "legend rule."" Card text names it, so it is a named row rather than part of
# `legendary`. Scoped to players, so "you" is the player, as in `playerDamageLifeLoss`. Each name
# two or more of them have in common is one group; the player chooses one permanent of each group,
# and the rest are put into their owners' graveyards together, as one event [CR#704.3]. Two
# permanents have the same name if they have at least one name in common, and one with no name
# shares none [CR#201.2a], so a legendary permanent that shares its name with no other is in no
# group and is not chosen. A permanent with two names is in two groups, so with two fully unlocked
# copies of one Room under *Leyline of Singularity* [CR#709.5] a player can choose a different
# copy for each name, leaving neither unchosen, where [CR#704.5j] keeps one
# (`syl-legend-rule-multiname-groups`).
sba legendRule {
  lexical = {lemma = "legend rule"},
  spelling = "legend rule",
  body = {
    scope = isPlayer,
    when = thereAre(
      withTheSameName(counted(orMore(2), and([hasSupertype(legendary), isPermanent, youControl])))),
    then = sequentially([
        doForEachKind(
          name,
          allOf(
            and([
                hasSupertype(legendary),
                isPermanent,
                youControl,
                shares(
                  cardName,
                  share,
                  a(and([isOther, hasSupertype(legendary), isPermanent, youControl])))])),
          cardName,
          choose(a(and([hasSupertype(legendary), isPermanent, youControl, named(chosenName)])))),
        putInto(
          each(
            and([
                hasSupertype(legendary),
                isPermanent,
                youControl,
                shares(
                  cardName,
                  share,
                  a(and([isOther, hasSupertype(legendary), isPermanent, youControl]))),
                notChosen])),
          graveyard)])}
}
